+detail = """One file per review scope under docs/reviews/rollup/<train>.md, compiled from the round files that scope carries: ordinal, phase, reviewed sha, parsed verdict word, finding count and filename, one row each. The scope is the TRAIN and not the work item, because a traincar is one review scope - a worker schedules its round only once every assigned item is built and the round covers the combined train diff, so a per-item rollup would have to invent a slice of a round that does not exist. Declared in the toolchain file's generated section, regenerated by the trunk step, freshness-gated by --check at the commit floor, and standing down on a work branch with the rest of the trunk-owned artifacts - the one member of that set whose SOURCE a branch necessarily writes, since the round files are a lane's own committed evidence. --check reports an absent file, a diverged one and an EXTRA one, on normalized line endings. It names NO governing verdict: governing is tree identity, a question about a branch's current tree that can only be answered against a repository at a moment, so every row here is a fact about a file."""
+rationale = """The hand-authored per-item rollup was the merge gate's only input and nothing in the kit wrote it, so every mechanized lane stopped at a human - and because it paraphrased evidence that already existed, it was also the one artifact in the tree that was neither generated, checked nor declared while the doctrine everywhere else refuses that shape. Splitting the roles is what makes both halves honest: the gate reads the evidence, and the summary a human genuinely wants to read becomes derived state that cannot drift from it. Writing a governing verdict into the file would rebuild the retired artifact under a new name - a checked-in summary that reads as authority and is stale the moment the branch moves - so the file states facts about files and stops."""
